WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.409
Come with us now on a journey
through time and space...

2
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.293
...to the world of The Mighty Boosh.

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:15.250
# The Mighty Boosh
# Come with us to the Mighty Boosh

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.176
# The Mighty Boosh
# Come with us to the Mighty Boosh #

5
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.689
- Hey. Bollo.
- Howard.

6
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.618
- What are you up to tonight?
- DJing at Rollerdisco.

7
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.537
Oh. yeah? Yeah. I DJ myself.

8
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.857
- I never seen you.
- Well. you know. I keep it low key.

9
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.777
Work peripheries mainly. you know.

10
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.460
Teacher training colleges.
village fetes. that sort of thing.

11
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.174
Little tip for you. What I do.
I stick to classic jazz when I DJ. yeah?

12
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.292
And then. just when they're least expecting it.
drop some Weather Report in.

13
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.935
Ow! Blows their minds.
Might want to try that yourself.

14
00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.572
I have to go now.

15
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.133
See you later.

16
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.015
Idiot.

17
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.134
What's going on in here?

18
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.818
Jazz night. Monday night. you coming?

19
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.660
Oh. no way. I need this room tonight.

20
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.697
- Well. you can't have it.
- Why not?

21
00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.811
Take a look at my yearly planner.

22
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.612
- Oh. can't you cancel that?
- No. I can't cancel it.

23
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.129
I'll be letting a lot of people down
if I did that. wouldn't I?

24
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.330
A lot of people? Like who?

25
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.020
- Members of the Jazz Club.
- Members of the Jazz Club?

26
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.769
It's just you and that old gimmer Horace.
Oh. can't you blow him out?

27
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.051
No. I can't.
I'm all he's got since his wife left him. okay?

28
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.330
- He's on the edge as it is.
- All right.

29
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.770
- I'll have to ring the girls. tell them it's off.
- What?

30
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.654
Oh. just a couple of Gothic girls. you know.
Pretty sexy. two of them. two of us.

31
00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.293
Thought it might be fun. Don't worry about it.

32
00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.775
I'll go round theirs.
try my luck at the Gothic three-way.

33
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.653
Hi. Horace.
Jazz is off tonight. something's cropped up.

34
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.018
I don't think Horace is going to be able
to make it tonight.

35
00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.971
So I'm freed up. What time are the girls coming?

36
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.410
Yeah. the thing is. these are Goth girls.
so there might be a bit of a problem.

37
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.498
- Why?
- Well. you're gonna have to get a bit dark like me.

38
00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.576
Like you?
You're the least dark person I've ever met.

39
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.214
- You're like candy floss.
- You cut me open and I'm made of Black Jacks.

40
00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.571
- You're Fruit Salad. Vince. everyone knows that.
- It's not Vince. I've changed my name.

41
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.497
- What?
- It's Obsidian now.

42
00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.169
- Obsidian?
- Yeah. Obsidian Blackbird McNight.

43
00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.018
Whatever. Inside. I'm darker than you. Yeah?
There's a dark poetry to me. yes. sir.

44
00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.416
Yeah. you can blag all that internal stuff.
I'm talking about the look. you know.

45
00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.974
- I mean. what are we going to do with your hair?
- What's wrong with it?

46
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.217
- It's a bit thin. isn't it?
- It's not thin. it's fine.

47
00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.094
You're not joking.
Can't even feel it. it's like brown smoke.

48
00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.610
Look. my hair is soft and gentle.
I get a lot of compliments about it. Girls like it.

49
00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.174
Yeah. not Goth girls. though.

50
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.256
What am I going to do. then?
Can you help me out?

51
00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.449
I don't know.

52
00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.138
You must have something to boost it up.

53
00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.898
Come on. you got a BTEC National in hair design.

54
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.978
All right. But lucky for you. there's this.

55
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.297
Goth Juice. the most powerful hairspray
known to man.

56
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.217
Made from the tears of Robert Smith.

57
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.659
Give me some of that.

58
00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.419
Easy. you don't know
what you're dealing with here. Back off a bit.

59
00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.771
A bit more. all right. Now. throw me that satsuma.

60
00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.492
Wow. that is some pretty powerful hold.

61
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.895
Yeah. Right. use it sparingly. yeah?

62
00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.976
Help yourself to my wardrobe.
I'll meet you later on.

63
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.852
- What time?
- Midnight.

64
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:36.095
Hey. Naboo. I need a favour.

65
00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:39.895
I went to the Black Spider last night
and met these beautiful Goth girls. yeah?

66
00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.615
The thing is. I got drunk.
I kind of told them I was a warlock.

67
00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.015
So. I was just wondering.
you haven't got any magic spells

68
00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.813
or any tricks or anything. you know.
that I can impress them with?

69
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.215
Vince. I'd love to help you
but I'm banned by shamanic law

70
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.490
to only use my power for a noble cause.

71
00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.930
Get lost! I've seen you on your magic carpet
when you can't get a taxi.

72
00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.130
- You've seen nothing.
- I've seen everything.

73
00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.933
You try Zingo and if that don't work.
you're on the rug.

74
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.698
Yeah. don't tell anyone about that. will you?

75
00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:05.936
All right. I won't. but maybe you can help me out.

76
00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.052
- All right. come on.
- Yes. Cheers. Naboo.

77
00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.693
Kalamanoohuh!

78
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.614
- This is my library of magic books.
- Wow.

79
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.015
- What's this?
- That's Houdini's diary.

80
00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.131
I bet that lets you into a few secrets.

81
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.410
I don't know. I can't get it open.

82
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.373
- Look at this one.
- Don't touch that.

83
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:29.459
- All right. easy.
- This is black magic. This is hardcore.

84
00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.219
- Don't mess with the occult.
- I thought it was good for you.

85
00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.410
- What?
- You know. good for your digestive system.

86
00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.929
- That's Yakult.
- Oh. yeah.

87
00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.335
- You ready? Cab's here.
- Yeah.

88
00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.734
Good.

89
00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.579
This is beige magic. It's more your level.

90
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.214
Oh. cheers. Naboo. You're a diamond.

91
00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.736
Do you like my new watch?

92
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.418
Nice. where did you get it?

93
00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:04.893
Topgoth.

94
00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.409
So are you really a sorcerer. then?

95
00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.734
Yeah.

96
00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:12.177
- When are we going to do some sorcery?
- Right now.

97
00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.254
Just going to call up my assistant.

98
00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.372
Ladies.

99
00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.049
Anthrax. Ebola.

100
00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.172
Howard Moon.

101
00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.614
- He's pretty dark.
- I'm the Dark Side of the Moon.

102
00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.653
That's one of mine.

103
00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.218
Howard. can I have a word?

104
00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.614
- I can't...
- What are you doing?

105
00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.332
I can't breathe.

106
00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:44.334
These are Goth girls. yeah?
They don't like jokes. they don't even smile. yeah?

107
00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:47.258
Do some dark stuff. freak them out a bit.

108
00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.377
- Went to a graveyard today.
- Yeah?

109
00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.616
Yeah. Got naked.

110
00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:57.016
Did a shit on a tombstone.

111
00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.056
Have you got the book. Howard?

112
00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:03.250
- There you go. Vince.
- Vince?

113
00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.178
I mean Obsidian Raven McBovril...

114
00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.768
- Obsidian Blackbird McNight.
- McNight.

115
00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.652
Thank you.

116
00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.613
Prepare yourselves for some powerful magic.

117
00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.975
I've seen his work. he's pretty good.

118
00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.818
- Do you mind?
- Sorry.

119
00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.776
- Is this a joke?
- Erm...

120
00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.097
Yeah. it's just a joke. It's the wrong book.

121
00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:34.937
I'll just go and get the proper one.

122
00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.416
Howard. you keep things ticking along here. yeah?
I think we're well in.

123
00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.451
I killed a swan yesterday.

124
00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.332
Did a shit on it.

125
00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:53.973
Right on it.

126
00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.530
I'll go and check on the sorcerer.
see how he's getting on.

127
00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.689
Vince.

128
00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.617
Well done. Ali Bongo. This is going well. isn't it?

129
00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:07.934
I'm dying on my arse out there.

130
00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.812
- What do you expect?
- What do you mean?

131
00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.817
- You could have shaved your moustache off.
- Why?

132
00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:14.215
Goths don't have moustaches.
You look like Tom Selleck.

133
00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.251
This is going nowhere. okay?
I'm bringing the moustache back.

134
00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.574
- Really?
- Yeah.

135
00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.498
Don't worry about it. all right.
because I've got an idea.

136
00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.895
Hey. isn't that Naboo's book of black magic?

137
00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:26.330
- I thought you were dark.
- I am. but that's stealing.

138
00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.652
Right. then.
You girls ready for something pretty dark?

139
00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.054
Whatever.

140
00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.574
Vince. I'm not sure about this.

141
00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.851
What's wrong. Howard? You scared?

142
00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.175
No.

143
00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.499
Hello. dear.

144
00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.576
An old lady? I'm terrified.

145
00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.292
This is rubbish.

146
00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.651
Don't go. That's the thing with summoning.
you don't know who you're going to get.

147
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.692
It's like lucky dip.
One week you get an old lady. the next week...

148
00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.970
- Yeah. I mean. who did we have last week?
- Hitler.

149
00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.614
Hitler. yeah. we played Pictionary with him.
He was a right laugh.

150
00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.812
- He couldn't draw to save his life.
- I did a shit on him.

151
00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:24.298
Well done. I knew it.
You always have to spoil it. don't you?

152
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.978
I knew I should have gone
for the Gothic three-way.

153
00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.534
It's not my fault.
You summoned up Granny Scroggins.

154
00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.059
Where is she?

155
00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.659
- It's Naboo.
- Go on. put his book back or he'll kill you.

156
00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.577
- Where's it gone?
- I don't know.

157
00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.134
- What are we going to do?
- Act natural.

158
00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:45.129
The thing I like about jazz was the movement
from bebop to modal jazz in the late '50s.

159
00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.979
where they made more of a use
of the flat nine chord.

160
00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.852
- Very fascinating.
- And...

161
00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.299
- Hey. guys.
- Hey!

162
00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.698
- How was the Rollerdisco?
- I was on fire. banging out tune after tune.

163
00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.130
- Yeah. Drop any weather report?
- Get stuffed.

164
00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.375
Fair enough.

165
00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.697
Naboo. you are looking good today.
You been working out?

166
00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:04.333
You're looking taut. fit and svelte.

167
00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.371
We love you. Naboo.
I don't know if we mentioned that.

168
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.968
Love what you're about. you know.
all the aspects of you.

169
00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:12.456
- You're a powerful character.
- Have you been going through my stuff?

170
00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:16.452
- No.
- I knew it. I told you not to mess with the occult.

171
00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.174
- Sorry about that.
- What have you done?

172
00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:22.576
- We might have summoned up a tiny demon.
- Demonette.

173
00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.577
I don't believe this.

174
00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:31.294
Hey. Naboo. sorry about that.

175
00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.138
- Get out.
- Oh. come on. Naboo.

176
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.093
You've gone too far this time.
I'm going to have to turn my back on you.

177
00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.173
- Sorry. Naboo.
- Come on. don't be like that.

178
00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:53.933
Let that be a lesson to you.
Right. let's sort this mess out.

179
00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.338
This is Spotlight for Demons. They're all in here.

180
00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:03.213
- What are we looking for? Horns?
- No.

181
00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:06.218
- Green skin?
- Not really. Just a little old lady.

182
00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.570
- What?
- A harmless old woman. you know.

183
00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:09.689
Not this one?

184
00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.493
Yeah. that's her.
I was getting quite a good vibe off her. actually.

185
00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.088
- You summoned Nanatoo.
- Nanatoo?

186
00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:21.691
She's the evilest demon known to man.
She's got five stars.

187
00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.139
Is that bad?

188
00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.728
We're going to have to reverse the spell.
Where's the book?

189
00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:29.409
Right. er...have you got a copy of that book?

190
00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.690
-7.000 years old.
- Right.

191
00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.380
Yeah. Naboo. you might want to start
backing your stuff up.

192
00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.456
I don't think you realise what you've done.

193
00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.969
If Nanatoo gets the book. she's going to multiply.

194
00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:41.056
Raise an evil army of Nanas.

195
00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.377
There'll be blood on the streets.
there'll be fire in the sky.

196
00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.377
You know what this means?

197
00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.819
Nanageddon!

198
00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.696
- Excuse me.
- What do you want. Wrinkles?

199
00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.098
When you are the moon.

200
00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:19.610
the best for you can be is a full moon...

201
00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.859
and then a half moon. he's all right.

202
00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.369
But the full moon is the famous moon.

203
00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.219
and. like. three quarters.

204
00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.490
no one gives a shit about him.

205
00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:36.455
When does he come?
Two days into the calendar month. He's useless.

206
00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.569
Full moon. the moon.

207
00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.819
The main moon.

208
00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:52.177
It saddens me to see you
under these circumstances. Naboo.

209
00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:54.814
You have been summoned
before the Board of Shaman

210
00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.056
for the most grievous of crimes.

211
00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:01.458
You let the book of spells
fall into the hands of the demon Nanatoo.

212
00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.457
This is Nanageddon.

213
00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.252
- It's Nanageddon.
- Nanageddon.

214
00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:08.338
- Nanageddon.
- I wasn't even there. I was DJing with Bollo.

215
00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.657
- DJing with your familiar?
- Highly unorthodox behaviour. Naboo.

216
00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:12.974
Even for you.

217
00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.251
These two guys I live with.
they tried to use the book to impress these girls.

218
00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.575
Oh. I'm Naboo. Nothing is ever my fault.

219
00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.019
What's it go to do with you?

220
00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:22.290
It's got everything to do with me.
and more to boot.

221
00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.853
- You've never liked me. have you?
- No.

222
00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.732
- And you're perfect?
- I'm pretty good.

223
00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.328
I've seen your CV. there's nothing on it.
I live my life.

224
00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.338
Live your life?
You live with a couple of doss bags and an ape.

225
00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.571
- What? You are an ape.
- Oh. well. yeah.

226
00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:37.692
Yeah. you've read all the books.
but when it comes to the crunch. where are you?

227
00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.412
The crunch?
How dare you speak to me of the crunch?

228
00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.213
You know nothing of the crunch.
you've never even been to the crunch.

